  "narrative": "The new discovery batch mostly gives null or subthreshold associations after signed-direction interpretation. H13 tests feature_003 in the feature_031=1 subgroup: estimate +0.004 with a wide interval centered near zero, so there is no support for a threshold-exceeding subgroup difference. H14 is the only candidate: feature_003 in older participants (feature_019 >=60) has a signed mean difference of +0.264, above the 0.15 threshold, and the 95% interval excludes zero (+0.122 to +0.405). However, the lower bound is below the scientific threshold and the result arises after multiple feature_003/subgroup and interaction probes; cell sizes are adequate but modest (108 vs 429). Therefore it is not yet strong enough for acceptance. I request independent validation of H14 because if the older-subgroup feature_003 association replicates with a threshold-supporting independent interval, it would justify accepting a dataset-specific older-subgroup mean-difference claim; if it fails, feature_003 should probably remain closed. H25 is related to H14 but tests age modification as an interaction: +0.159, lower bound -0.016. It is near the point threshold but too imprecise and includes no interaction, so I keep it deferred rather than accepting it. H26 does not support feature_038-based modification. The marker interaction tests are also weak: H15 is opposite the claimed direction, and H27-H31 are small or wide around null, so I close them. H16 and H24 are screening contrasts and are not meaningful. Overall, no claim is accepted yet; validation of H14 is the most useful next step while the remaining binary/ordinal scan continues in later rounds.",
  "research_notes": "After iteration 2 discoveries: H14 is the only active near-threshold candidate: feature_003 older-subgroup mean difference R15 +0.264 (CI +0.122 to +0.405), signed positive. Validation requested for H14. Do not accept before independent validation unless the validation evidence is clearly threshold-supportive. If H14 validation supports threshold, accept H14 only as an observational older-subgroup association in this dataset and consider complement/younger-age tests or adjusted/stratified checks for confounding. If H14 fails, close feature_003 family including H25 unless a new strong refinement emerges. H25 remains deferred because it is conceptually linked to H14 but its interval does not exclude no interaction. H13, H26, H15, H27-H31, H16, and H24 are closed null/subthreshold. Next iterations: assess validation of H14 in synthesis; continue untested claims H17-H23 and H32-H36; avoid low-prevalence H6 unless a new strong subgroup appears; watch for multiplicity and do not interpret associations as causal."
